1
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:12,001
Your broker shows gold at 2652. On futures, the same gold is at 2668.

2
00:00:12,451 --> 00:00:17,857
A sixteen point gap. Put the level in the wrong place, and the whole plan is wrong.

3
00:00:18,308 --> 00:00:24,839
Today: a practical order flow setup for gold and forex. Module five begins.

4
00:00:25,839 --> 00:00:30,750
Hello, this is episode twenty one of the SPIDER Order Flow series.

5
00:00:31,200 --> 00:00:36,921
Last time: failed auctions, single prints, and poor highs.

6
00:00:37,371 --> 00:00:42,438
So far we learned the tools. Now we learn to set them up properly on screen.

7
00:00:43,438 --> 00:00:51,066
Remember episode six. Spot gold and forex have no single exchange, nobody has the real volume.

8
00:00:51,516 --> 00:00:56,114
The broker's volume is just tick volume, meaning how many times price moved.

9
00:00:56,564 --> 00:01:02,128
Real contracts, delta, footprint: all of that comes from the futures exchange.

10
00:01:03,128 --> 00:01:08,378
So the setup has two parts. On the left, futures, where you read order flow.

11
00:01:08,827 --> 00:01:12,877
On the right, the broker's spot chart, where the trade actually happens.

12
00:01:13,327 --> 00:01:19,205
Read on futures, trade on spot. The thing that links them is the basis.

13
00:01:20,205 --> 00:01:30,079
Basis is the gap between futures and spot. Right now futures 2668.4, spot 2652.1.

14
00:01:30,529 --> 00:01:36,562
So the basis is plus 16.3. It comes from interest and time.

15
00:01:37,012 --> 00:01:42,160
It changes slowly, so measure it once at the start of every day.

16
00:01:43,160 --> 00:01:47,365
Say futures shows a poor high at 2670.

17
00:01:47,815 --> 00:01:54,658
On spot, that level is 2670 minus 16.3, which is 2653.7.

18
00:01:55,109 --> 00:02:00,256
Put that level on the broker chart. Forget the basis, and you are sixteen points off.

19
00:02:01,256 --> 00:02:09,144
Forex works the same way. For EURUSD use Euro futures; both move in the same direction.

20
00:02:09,594 --> 00:02:17,483
But for USDJPY, Yen futures move the opposite way. USDJPY up, Yen futures down.

21
00:02:17,933 --> 00:02:23,888
There, buying in futures means selling in USDJPY. Remember that flip.

22
00:02:24,888 --> 00:02:30,375
Watch the clock too. Futures take a break of about an hour every day.

23
00:02:30,825 --> 00:02:37,251
Liquidity is thin before and after the break. Delta there is not reliable.

24
00:02:37,701 --> 00:02:42,220
The clearest picture comes at the London and New York opens.

25
00:02:43,220 --> 00:02:51,658
Now the tools. Only four are essential: volume profile, VWAP, footprint, and delta.

26
00:02:52,108 --> 00:02:58,638
Profile and VWAP give the level. Footprint and delta give the confirmation.

27
00:02:59,089 --> 00:03:05,515
Ten more indicators are just noise. The fuller the screen, the slower the decision.

28
00:03:06,515 --> 00:03:11,844
A clean layout: top left, the futures footprint; below it, delta.

29
00:03:12,293 --> 00:03:18,250
On the right, the spot chart with only the converted levels and VWAP.

30
00:03:18,700 --> 00:03:23,454
And the basis number in one corner, so the math is always in front of you.

31
00:03:24,454 --> 00:03:30,096
Common mistakes. One: treating broker tick volume as real volume.

32
00:03:30,546 --> 00:03:38,670
Two: forgetting the basis. Three: reading direction wrong on an inverted pair like the Yen.

33
00:03:39,120 --> 00:03:42,829
And four: trading in the thin hours around the break.

34
00:03:43,829 --> 00:03:48,898
So, today in short. Read order flow on futures, trade on spot.

35
00:03:49,347 --> 00:03:55,067
To convert a level, subtract the basis from the futures level. Measure the basis daily.

36
00:03:55,518 --> 00:04:01,239
Pairs like the Yen move inverted. Four tools are enough, the rest is noise.

37
00:04:02,239 --> 00:04:08,509
Next episode: the top-down method. Context, then level, then confirmation.

38
00:04:08,959 --> 00:04:13,791
If this was useful, subscribe and save the playlist.

39
00:04:14,241 --> 00:04:19,492
Our Telegram and Instagram are in the description. See you in the next episode.

